From 2cf222ecd3a55f86ed808ebdb7ecfea794e45924 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pieroviano <piero.viano@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 19:40:57 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Re-parent DataGridViewRow/Cell onto DataGridViewBand/Element

Closes the last substantive gap in API-COMPLETENESS.md. DataGridViewElement (the
base of bands and cells) and DataGridViewBand (the base of rows and columns) were
absent, so `is DataGridViewBand` and the element hierarchy did not exist. Add both
and re-parent DataGridViewRow : DataGridViewBand : DataGridViewElement and
DataGridViewCell : DataGridViewElement.

The three feared conflicts were reconciled with the override approach rather than
a state-model rewrite: the bases declare the shared members as virtual, and each
leaf overrides the ones it already implements, so behaviour is unchanged - Row's
State stays computed from its flags (not Element's stored source), and Cell's
DataGridView stays computed from OwningRow. Row additionally inherits the band
members it lacked (Tag, IsRow, HasDefaultCellStyle, DefaultHeaderCellType, the
element raisers), closing member gaps too (net48 8026->7953, DataGridViewRow now
17/59). DataGridViewColumn : TreeViewColumn (a GTK base) stays as-is and does not
derive from Band - a documented partial, the one conflict overrides cannot fix.

Covered by DataGridViewBandFunctionalTests (hierarchy, State still computes from
the flags after the move, inherited band surface). Full Forms suite green at 2500,
Drawing at 1216.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
